# API Patterns

## authHttpClient

All authenticated API calls use `authHttpClient` (Axios instance from `@src/api/authHttpClient`).
It auto-attaches `Authorization: Bearer <token>` and handles 401 → sign out.

## Company Header

Company-scoped endpoints require a custom header:

```tsx
function withCompany(companyId: number) {
  return { company: String(companyId) };
}

const { data } = await authHttpClient.get('/attendance/list', {
  headers: withCompany(companyId),
  params: { ... },
});
```

## API Module Pattern

Group related endpoints in a single object per domain:

```tsx
export const attendanceApi = {
  async getAttendanceList(companyId: number, params: Params): Promise<Response> {
    const { data } = await authHttpClient.get<Response>('/attendance/list', {
      headers: withCompany(companyId),
      params: { ... },
    });
    return data;
  },
  async markAttendance(companyId: number, payload: Payload): Promise<Response> { ... },
};
```

## Error Handling

Use `readApiError(err)` from `@src/utils/readApiError` to extract a user-facing message from Axios errors. It checks `response.data.message`, `response.data.error`, then falls back to `err.message`.
